  "note": "Election of the Limavady Urban District Council, nominations 5 January 1923; only six candidates for nine seats, so all were returned without a contest (Belfast Telegraph, 6 January 1923, p. 6). Only six nominations were received for nine seats, so the six nominated candidates were declared elected without a contest; the report adds that the remaining three vacancies were filled by the automatic election of the three councillors with the largest poll at the previous contest, Messrs Coghlan, Hunt and Duddy. The Londonderry Sentinel of the same date prints the same six nominations and gives Colonel Macrory's initials as F. B. N. No party label was printed. Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of the Belfast Telegraph, 6 January 1923, p. 6 (council-audit, Nov 2026): Colonel Macrory's initials are F. S. N. as printed (were F. B. N.), as the Ballymoney Free Press, 14 January 1926, p. 2 also prints them."
